WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.284 --> 00:00:17.890
On the to Lady Katherine's home, Mandy introduced herself.

2
00:00:19.131 --> 00:00:21.472
Then she asked: "Where am I?"

3
00:00:22.592 --> 00:00:26.694
Lady Katherine thought Mandy was confused after her accident.

4
00:00:26.714 --> 00:00:31.316
"Why, child, you're in London, England.

5
00:00:31.952 --> 00:00:37.016
Elizabeth is our queen," said Lady Katherine in a comforting way.

6
00:00:38.297 --> 00:00:41.499
Mandy had read about Elizabeth I of England.

7
00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.502
She thought it would be great to actually meet her.

8
00:00:45.522 --> 00:00:49.265
"Is the queen as kind as people say?"

9
00:00:49.885 --> 00:00:50.646
asked Mandy.

10
00:00:50.666 --> 00:00:55.809
"Her majesty is good and fair," replied Lady Katherine.

11
00:00:55.829 --> 00:00:59.072
"England has never been so peaceful."

12
00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:01.780
Mandy looked outside.

13
00:01:02.321 --> 00:01:04.361
She noticed how busy the streets were.

14
00:01:05.542 --> 00:01:09.123
Women wore long dresses and some carried baskets.

15
00:01:10.023 --> 00:01:13.204
Men wore fancy hats decorated with feathers.

16
00:01:14.404 --> 00:01:16.665
Horses and carriages filled the streets.

17
00:01:19.725 --> 00:01:21.826
They arrived at Lady Katherine's home.

18
00:01:22.566 --> 00:01:24.067
A servant opened the door.

19
00:01:24.087 --> 00:01:28.328
"The girl has been hurt," Lady Katherine said.

20
00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:30.561
"Please take care of her."

21
00:01:32.482 --> 00:01:36.465
When her knee was cleaned up, Mandy was led into a big room.

22
00:01:37.446 --> 00:01:42.169
Two other servants brought trays of cakes, gingerbread, and almond milk.

23
00:01:42.189 --> 00:01:45.411
"Thank you," she said to them.

24
00:01:46.412 --> 00:01:47.933
The servants smiled at her.

25
00:01:47.953 --> 00:01:52.096
"Have you been with Lady Katherine a long time?"

26
00:01:52.896 --> 00:01:53.617
asked Mandy.

27
00:01:53.637 --> 00:01:59.969
"Our family has always served Lady Katherine's family," said one servant.

28
00:01:59.989 --> 00:02:04.010
"Oh! Do you like to work for Lady Katherine?"

29
00:02:04.631 --> 00:02:05.391
asked Mandy.

30
00:02:05.411 --> 00:02:08.832
"Lady Katherine is very good to us.

31
00:02:09.473 --> 00:02:13.795
We are treated like part of the family," replied the other servant.

32
00:02:14.875 --> 00:02:19.217
Meanwhile, Vinnie and Edward were having lunch with Master Crossland.

33
00:02:20.097 --> 00:02:23.039
The tailor and his family lived above the shop.

34
00:02:24.019 --> 00:02:26.120
They all shared one small room.

35
00:02:27.348 --> 00:02:34.312
"If you're looking for work," said the tailor, nodding to Vinnie, "I could use your help today."

36
00:02:35.413 --> 00:02:38.835
Vinnie looked at Edward, and the boy nodded, smiling.

37
00:02:38.855 --> 00:02:41.917
"Sure," Vinnie replied.

38
00:02:42.497 --> 00:02:43.838
He ate some more bread.

39
00:02:46.339 --> 00:02:50.802
After the meal, Master Crossland took the boys back down to the shop.

40
00:02:51.822 --> 00:02:54.584
He showed Vinnie how to cut some cotton cloth.

41
00:02:55.772 --> 00:02:57.733
Vinnie had to be very careful.

42
00:02:57.753 --> 00:03:00.795
"Oops! I cut too much!"

43
00:03:01.615 --> 00:03:02.396
Vinnie cried.

44
00:03:02.416 --> 00:03:07.098
"You'll get better with practice," said the tailor.

45
00:03:08.219 --> 00:03:10.240
Vinnie had trouble cutting the cloth.

46
00:03:11.301 --> 00:03:13.182
But Edward was very good at it.

47
00:03:13.202 --> 00:03:19.345
"You will make a fine tailor one day," Master Crossland said to Edward.

48
00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:24.868
"Maybe I can make the costumes for the Globe Theater," said Edward.

49
00:03:25.724 --> 00:03:33.548
"Then I could meet Shakespeare and "Get those crazy ideas out of your head," said the tailor.

50
00:03:33.568 --> 00:03:36.950
"Working at the Globe will not feed your family."

51
00:03:38.671 --> 00:03:42.013
Suddenly, a well-dressed man came into the shop.

52
00:03:42.973 --> 00:03:45.035
He wore a cloak with a high collar.

53
00:03:46.755 --> 00:03:48.176
"Welcome, Lord Crumley!"

54
00:03:48.696 --> 00:03:49.517
said the tailor.

55
00:03:49.537 --> 00:03:53.079
"Lads, bring me those three rolls of silk!"

56
00:03:53.659 --> 00:03:54.960
He pointed to a corner.

57
00:03:56.324 --> 00:03:58.606
Edward and Vinnie went to get the silk.

58
00:03:58.626 --> 00:04:01.508
"Quick," said the lord.

59
00:04:01.528 --> 00:04:02.829
"I'm in a hurry!"

60
00:04:03.369 --> 00:04:05.391
He frowned as he took off his cloak.

61
00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:08.913
Lord Crumley was a very rich man.

62
00:04:09.934 --> 00:04:12.076
But he did not seem very kind.
